		336 -> 347;
	341 [label="Mm. Yes. Marie told me of this. You do not believe in the workings of invisible forces in our world - including that of the Indifference. Is that so?",shape=box,color=blue];
		341 -> 352;
		341 -> 353;
	340 [label="Intriguing. This is the second time I have gleaned the impression from you that you do not seem to hold faith in the reality of your Indifference. Is that so?",shape=box,color=blue];
		340 -> 350;
		340 -> 351;
	339 [label="Intriguing. Do I glean from you that your own faith has been shaken as of late? Or have you never had any in your Indifference to begin with?",shape=box,color=blue];
		339 -> 350;
		339 -> 351;
	337 [label="I'm not sure the Indifference was real until we made it real. I think we conjured it just the same way I conjured Duviri.",shape=box,color=red];
		337 -> 348;
	338 [label="I do think the Indifference is a real deity - with a real sentience behind it.",shape=box,color=red];
		338 -> 349;
	342 [label="Sometimes, I wonder if that is not the reason why so many turn to faith at the end of the day...",shape=box,color=blue];
		342 -> 354;
	343 [label="Pardon, but I begin to worry when any individual feels \"justified\" in any action, especially when it comes to predicting the motivations of others.",shape=box,color=blue];
		343 -> 355;
		343 -> 356;
	344 [label="Should we be concerned about what may happen when it moves on to the less obvious parts?",shape=box,color=blue];
		344 -> 357;
	345 [label="I think the Indifference is trying to learn to be \"human.\" It was always something Bigger. Different. So it's learning how to exist as something Smaller, and Us.",shape=box,color=red];
		345 -> 358;
	346 [label="Sometimes I wonder if the Indifference never really had a body of its own before we interacted with it. So it's learning how to exist.",shape=box,color=red];
